This C program reads the current from an MLX91219 Hall-Effect Current Sensor using an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1. It configures the ADS1115 for single-shot mode, single-ended input on AIN0, a programmable gain of ±4.096V, and a data rate of 128 SPS. It then reads the 16-bit conversion result every 500 ms, converts it to amperes, and logs the current value to the console. It handles I2C write and read errors and the case where the sensor is absent. On receipt of SIGINT, it closes the I2C handle and invokes the library's cleanup API call before exiting.

