This C program reads analog values from two Seeed Studio Grove Moisture Sensors connected to an MCP3008 ADC on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It initializes the SPI bus, reads sensor values every 5 seconds, logs the readings with timestamps to a file named `moisture_log.csv`, and handles errors gracefully. On receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, it ensures that the SPI file descriptors and driver library resources are released.

