This C program interfaces with a Melexis MLX91211 Triaxis Current Sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0, using CE0 on GPIO8 (BCM), SCLK on GPIO11 (BCM), MOSI on GPIO10 (BCM) and MISO on GPIO9 (BCM). It samples the current once every second, converts the ADC reading to amperes, writes a line containing a timestamp and the current in amperes to a file named `current_log.csv`, checks all open, ioctl, read and file I/O calls for errors and retries any SPI communication failures up to three times. It also implements error handling and graceful termination by catching SIGINT and SIGTERM to close file descriptors and release GPIO lines cleanly. If the measured current exceeds 10.0 A, the software drives GPIO17 low to disable the motor, logs the over-current event, waits one second, then drives GPIO17 high to re-enable the motor, and continues normal sampling thereafter.

