This C program continuously reads the analog output of a Honeywell MICROceL MCO-S4 CO sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 (1 MHz, mode 0) using CE0 on GPIO 8 (BCM), SCLK on GPIO 11 (BCM), MOSI on GPIO 10 (BCM), and MISO on GPIO 9 (BCM). It samples channel 0 once per second, logs the timestamp and voltage to a file named `co_log.txt` in the specified format, checks the return values of the required library API calls and the SPI transfer function, and handles errors appropriately. It also drives GPIO 4 HIGH when the measured voltage exceeds 2.5 V and LOW otherwise, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, it closes the SPI handle, closes the log file, turns off the alarm, and invokes the appropriate library cleanup call.

