This C program interfaces with an ADXL335 accelerometer using an MCP3008 ADC on the SPI0 bus of a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the X, Y, and Z axes from the ADC channels 0, 1, and 2, respectively, at a sampling rate of 100 Hz. The raw ADC values are logged to a file named `impact_log.txt` with timestamped, comma-separated entries. If the ADC value for any axis exceeds a configurable impact threshold, a line containing "IMPACT DETECTED" is written to the log file. The program ensures proper initialization, error checking, and cleanup on all exit paths, including handling a SIGINT signal.

