This C program reads Heart Rate and SpO₂ data from a Silicon Labs Si1172-A30-GMR Optical Heart Rate Sensor on I2C bus 1, samples once per second, and logs each sample to a file named `biometric_log.csv`. It checks the return value of every driver library I2C call, distinguishes transient I2C errors from a completely absent or uninitialized sensor, and when a read fails, writes a row with the appropriate error flag instead of crashing. The program also handles SIGINT (Ctrl-C) to perform a graceful shutdown that closes the I2C handle, terminates the driver library, and closes the log file.

