This C program continuously monitors a potted plant using a HiLetgo Soil Moisture Sensor connected to the MCP3008 ADC on the SPI bus CE0 (bus 0, channel 0) operating at 500 kHz in single-ended mode. It logs a timestamped moisture percentage to a file named `plant_data.txt` in append mode every 60 seconds in the specified format. The program accepts command-line arguments to specify the SPI channel, ADC channel, minimum and maximum calibration values, the moisture threshold, the logging interval, the recipient email address, and the path to an msmtp configuration file. It checks every initialization call and each SPI transfer for errors, printing diagnostics to stderr. It handles a failed ADC read by logging the error to stderr and simply retrying on the next cycle without crashing. It triggers an email alert via msmtp whenever the measured moisture falls below the specified threshold (or 30% if not specified), validates the msmtp exit status, and cleanly handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by closing the SPI interface, terminating the driver, freeing any dynamically allocated memory, and exiting cleanly on all exit paths.

