This C program continuously monitors soil moisture using a Keyes KY-036 analog sensor connected to an MCP3008 10-bit SPI ADC on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It opens SPI0 on CE0 (GPIO8) at 1 MHz in mode 0, samples the sensor once per second by default (or an interval specified by the user via `argv[1]`), and logs each reading to `soil_moisture.log` with an ISO-8601 timestamp, the raw 10-bit ADC value, and the calculated moisture percentage. It rigorously checks for errors in ADC initialization, SPI device open, SPI transfers, and file I/O operations, logging warnings and continuing if the sensor is absent or a bus error occurs. A signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM ensures clean shutdown by closing the SPI handle, flushing and closing the log file, and invoking the ADC's cleanup routine before exiting. The implementation reads the analog output via the MCP3008 channel 0 without using any driver library.

