This C program continuously reads the analog output of an MQ-2 gas sensor through an MCP3008 ADC connected on SPI0 using CE0 (GPIO8, BCM) and channel 0, sampling every 500 ms. It drives an active buzzer attached to GPIO24 (BCM) so that the buzzer is turned off when the ADC reading is below the threshold value of 500 and turned on when the reading is equal to or exceeds 500. It verifies that the driver library initializes correctly, validates that the SPI handle is obtained and that each read operation succeeds, and checks that each GPIO write succeeds. It also handles a SIGINT (Ctrl-C) by closing the SPI handle, resetting the GPIO states to a safe condition, and invoking the library’s cleanup API call().

