This C program continuously reads the analog output of a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0, compares the reading to a configurable threshold, activates a relay-driven water pump on GPIO 18 when the moisture level falls below the threshold, and logs every moisture reading and each pump activation or deactivation with timestamps to a file named `irrigation.log`. It handles command-line options for threshold, pump duration, and sleep interval, retries SPI communication errors up to three times, and ensures the pump is turned off on all exit paths, including any failure to open the SPI bus.

