This C program continuously monitors the PCF8591 ADC's AIN0 channel over the I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1`, sampling every 100 ms. It performs a dummy read first and discards that byte, then reads the current 8-bit sample (0-255) and prints each value to stdout. The program checks the result of every I2C `ioctl`, `read`, and `write` call and terminates with a non-zero exit code on any failure. It also installs a SIGINT handler so that when the user presses Ctrl-C, the I2C file descriptor is cleanly closed before the program exits.

