This C program continuously reads the Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 CE0 configured at 1 MHz, SPI mode 0, using channel 0. It compares the 10-bit reading to a threshold of 300 every 60 seconds. When the value drops below this threshold, it activates a relay-driven water pump connected to GPIO18 (BCM numbering) for exactly 10 seconds, then deactivates it, while logging each watering event with a timestamp and the measured moisture level to a file named `watering_events.txt`. The program validates the selected ADC channel, checks the return status of every API call to the ADC and GPIO interfaces, detects and handles stuck or otherwise invalid ADC values, recovers gracefully from any GPIO initialization failure, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM immediately turns off the pump, releases all resources, and exits cleanly.

