This C program continuously monitors a Honeywell SS49E linear Hall-effect sensor using an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1. It reads the magnetic field strength in Gauss and prints it to the console every 100 ms. If the measured field exceeds a user-configurable threshold (default 100.0 Gauss), it blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 (BCM) with a 50 ms on/off duty cycle for 1 second. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure clean resource release on all exit paths.

