This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read an HL-69 analog soil moisture sensor using an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 with CE0 (GPIO8). It applies hysteresis control to a relay-driven pump on GPIO17 based on the moisture reading, publishes the moisture value every 60 seconds to the MQTT topic "soil_moisture", and subscribes to the MQTT topic "pump_control" to accept "pump_on" and "pump_off" commands. It includes robust error handling for SPI open or transfer failures, GPIO write failures, MQTT connection or subscription failures, and out-of-range sensor-absent conditions. All events are logged to syslog, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, the program cleanly turns the relay off, closes the SPI interface, disconnects from MQTT, and terminates the driver library.

