This C program continuously reads analog voltages from channels 0, 1, and 2 of an MCP3008 connected to SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It converts the 10-bit ADC values to voltages (assuming VREF = 3.3V) and appends a timestamped line with the three voltage readings to a CSV file named `sensor_data.csv` every 5 seconds. It verifies the initialization of the driver library, the opening of the SPI interface, the success of each SPI transfer, and the success of all file operations, handling any error by reporting it and aborting cleanly. It also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure that on termination, it releases all resources by closing the SPI device and shutting down the driver library before exiting.

