This C program continuously samples the output of a MAX9814 electret microphone amplifier connected to an MCP3008 ADC via the SPI0 CE0 bus on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It uses the sampled ambient noise level to modulate two 3V vibration motors with hardware PWM at 100Hz on GPIO17 and GPIO27. The motors are turned off when the noise level does not exceed a threshold of 500. Timestamps of any significant vibration events are logged to a file named `vibration_log.txt`. The program implements robust error handling for SPI initialization failures, ADC read errors, and file I/O problems. It ensures a graceful shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by stopping both motors, closing the SPI device, and terminating the driver cleanly.

