This C program continuously monitors an MQ-135 air quality sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected to SPI0 CE0 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the sensor voltage every 5 seconds, converts the ADC value to an estimated CO₂ concentration, and controls a ventilation fan attached to GPIO18 based on the CO₂ level. The program logs the timestamp, CO₂ ppm value, and fan state to a file named `air_quality.log` in CSV format. It handles SPI communication errors by retrying without crashing and gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by turning off the fan, closing the SPI interface, and releasing all driver resources before exiting.

