This C program reads three successive samples from a Vegetronix VH400 soil-moisture sensor using an MCP3008 ADC on SPI channel 0 (CE0 on GPIO8) with a 1 MHz clock and SPI mode 0. It computes the average of the three raw ADC values while skipping any individual read that fails, and uses that average to set the position of an ASCO RedHat 8210 series proportional solenoid valve connected to GPIO17 (BCM numbering) with PWM at 100 Hz and a duty-cycle range of 0-100. It logs every 5 seconds to a file named `irrigation.log` a timestamp together with the three raw ADC readings, the computed average, and the resulting valve position. Signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM provide a graceful shutdown by setting the valve PWM to 0, closing the SPI interface, closing the log file, and terminating the driver library.

