This C program continuously monitors an MQ-135 air quality sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI channel 0, configured at 1 MHz, mode 0, reading channel 0 every 5 seconds. It computes an AQI value and logs the timestamp and AQI to an append-mode file named "air_quality.log". The program activates a ventilation fan driven by a relay connected to GPIO18 (BCM) when the AQI exceeds 100 and deactivates it otherwise. It implements robust error handling for SPI communication failures by retrying up to three times with a 1-second delay between attempts and, if still failing, re-initializing the SPI interface before continuing. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown that turns the fan off, closes the SPI interface, closes the log file, and terminates the driver library, ensuring all resources are released on every exit path.

