Please note that this code assumes you have the `libgpiod` library installed on your Raspberry Pi. You can install it using `sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev`.

Also, the `spi_read` function is not defined in this code. You would need to implement or include a function that reads from the MCP3008 ADC using the SPI interface. This function should return the sensor value or -1 on error.

Lastly, this code does not handle the case where the SPI interface is not available or cannot be opened. You would need to add appropriate error handling for this scenario.

