This C program continuously reads the digital output (DO) of a KY-038 sound sensor module connected to GPIO17 (BCM numbering) and prints the sound level reading (0 or 1) to the console each loop iteration with a 100 ms delay between reads. When the sensor reports a sound event (DO pin goes LOW), it triggers an alarm LED attached to GPIO18 (BCM) by turning the LED on for 1 second and then off. The program verifies successful initialization of the GPIO driver, opening of the chip, line request, and checks the result of every I/O operation, handling sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully by printing an error message and exiting. It also catches SIGINT (Ctrl-C) or SIGTERM and cleanly releases all GPIO lines before exiting, ensuring proper resource cleanup on all exit paths.

