This C program continuously reads the analog output of a Keyes KY-038 sound sensor connected to channel 0 of an MCP3008 ADC over the SPI bus CE0 on GPIO 8 using mode 0 at 1 MHz, sampling every 10 ms. When the measured value exceeds a defined threshold, it turns on an LED wired to GPIO 16 (BCM) for 500 ms, logs the event with a timestamp in the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" to a file named `sound_events.log`, applies a debounce delay after each trigger, and gracefully handles any SPI transfer failures, invalid ADC channel selections, or GPIO initialization errors by checking all driver library calls and file operations. It also installs a SIGINT handler that on receipt cleanly releases resources by closing the SPI interface, terminating the driver library, and turning off the LED.

