This C program continuously monitors the analog output of a MAX9814 electret microphone amplifier using a bit-banged ADC sampling on BCM GPIO26. It detects a clap event, respecting a 50 ms debounce interval, and turns on an LED connected to BCM GPIO16 for 500 ms while printing a timestamped detection message to the console. It verifies that the ADC driver and GPIO mode settings are successfully initialized, handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully, and includes a SIGINT handler that, on Ctrl + C, turns off the LED and cleanly releases all resources. The implementation is written in C11 without using any deprecated APIs and runs until interrupted.

