This C program continuously reads the analog output of a TI DRV5055VA Hall-effect sensor through an MCP3008 ADC connected on SPI0 CE0 using the SPI pins GPIO8, GPIO9, GPIO10, and GPIO11. It samples the value on channel 0 every 100 ms, converts it to magnetic field strength, appends a timestamped reading to a file named `magnetic_log.txt`, and when the measured field exceeds a threshold of 10.0 mT, it turns on an LED wired to BCM GPIO21, turning it off otherwise. It verifies that the SPI interface opens successfully, that each ADC read returns valid data, and that the log file can be opened, handling any initialization failures appropriately. It also installs a SIGINT handler that performs graceful cleanup by closing the SPI connection, switching off the LED, and terminating the driver library before exiting.

