This C program reads an anemometer pulse on GPIO17 (BCM) using an interrupt on the rising edge, counts pulses over a 500 ms sample window to compute real-time wind speed, and reads wind direction from a wind vane connected to channel 0 of an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0/CE0 in mode 0 at 1 MHz. It updates a 16x2 LCD with a PCF8574 backpack on I2C bus 1 to display both wind speed and direction every 500 ms. It checks the result of every driver library, I2C, and SPI call, detecting sensor-absent conditions such as the ADC reading stuck at 0 or 1023 or any I2C/SPI failures, and printing diagnostic messages to stderr while continuing to run. Finally, it handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown that releases the SPI handle, the I2C handle, and any driver library resources.

