This C program continuously reads the distance from a TDK InvenSense ICU-20201 ultrasonic Time-of-Flight sensor on I2C bus 1, sampling every 100 ms. It drives an LED connected to GPIO 17 (BCM numbering) such that the LED is turned on when the measured distance is below 20 cm and off otherwise. It logs each distance reading together with an ISO-8601 timestamp to a file named `distance_log.txt`. The program checks the result of every I2C, driver library, and file operation, handles cases where the sensor is absent or the bus reports errors in a graceful manner, and ensures that all resources—including the I2C handle, the GPIO pin, and any driver state—are cleanly released on every exit path by handling SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

