This C program reads distance from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor connected to GPIO pins 17 (trigger) and 18 (echo) on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sends a 10 µs trigger pulse, waits for the echo rising and falling edges, and calculates the distance based on the duration of the echo pulse. It logs each valid measurement with a timestamp and handles errors such as driver initialization failure, echo-edge timeouts, and invalid pulse durations. The program also ensures graceful shutdown on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

Please note that the HC-SR04 operates at 5V, while the Raspberry Pi GPIO is only 3.3V tolerant. Therefore, a 1kΩ resistor must be used on the echo line to prevent damage to the GPIO pin. This is mentioned in the comments within the code.

