This C program interfaces with a TDK Chirp ICU-20201 ultrasonic time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1, reads the distance measurement every 100 ms, logs each distance together with an ISO 8601 timestamp to a file named `distance_log.txt`, and asserts a GPIO alert on physical pin 17 (BCM 17) when the measured distance falls below 10.0 cm. It handles all I2C read/write errors, detects the absence of the sensor, and manages any errors that occur while creating or writing the log file. It also cleanly releases all resources—including I2C handles, the GPIO pin, and any driver state—when receiving a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

