This C program interfaces two TCRT5000 IR obstacle avoidance sensors on the GPIO bus of a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It polls each sensor every 10ms, applies a 50ms software debounce per sensor, and logs every state transition to a file named `proximity_log.txt` with an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp, the sensor ID (1 or 2), and the event type ('DETECTED' for a HIGH-to-LOW transition indicating an obstacle and 'CLEARED' for a LOW-to-HIGH transition indicating clearance). It checks the return values of the library's API call() three times as required, verifies all file I/O operations, and on all exit paths—including graceful shutdown on SIGINT or SIGTERM—ensures clean resource release by closing the log file and calling the library's API call() to release the GPIO resources.

