This C program initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins for the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and the buzzer, and registers an interrupt function for the echo pin. It continuously sends a 10 µs HIGH pulse on the trigger pin, measures the echo time using the interrupt-driven API, computes the distance, and outputs it every 100 ms. It also handles sensor-absent conditions and invalid readings, activates the buzzer when the distance is less than 30 cm, and ensures a clean shutdown on SIGINT.

