This C program initializes the VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1, controls the XSHUT pin with GPIO27 (BCM) configured as an output and set high to enable the sensor (active-low trigger), repeatedly reads the distance every 100 ms, and logs each reading to the systemd journal via syslog including a timestamp, the measured distance in millimetres, and the sensor status, using LOG_INFO for successful reads and LOG_ERR for any read failures. It verifies that the driver library initializes correctly and that the I2C device can be opened, handles read errors by logging them and continuing the loop without crashing, and installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers that close the I2C handle, terminate the driver library, and exit cleanly.

