This C program interfaces with a Silicon Labs Si1182-A-GM optical sensor over I2C on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It verifies the sensor by reading its part ID register and configures the measurement rate register. It then continuously reads ambient light (lux) and proximity data every 100ms, logging each timestamped reading to a CSV line in a file named `biometric_log.txt` and printing the same line to stdout. It handles I2C read and write errors, sensor absence, and I2C bus errors. It also includes SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers to close the I2C file descriptor and the log file, ensuring all resources are released on normal and error exits.

