This C program initializes the pigpio library and sets up the GPIO pins for the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and the buzzer. It uses an interrupt-driven approach to measure the distance and activate the buzzer when the distance is below 20 cm. The program prints the distance to stdout every second and sets the buzzer pin high if the distance is under 20 cm, otherwise sets it low. It also handles SIGINT to ensure proper cleanup and termination.

