This C program sets up communication with a VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1, verifies the model ID, programs the timing budget, and starts ranging. It then repeatedly polls the 16-bit distance register and operates a servo-actuated gate connected to GPIO18 by setting a 1000 µs pulse width when the object is farther than 250 mm and a 2000 µs pulse width when it is closer than 200 mm, providing hysteresis. The program also logs the gate opening and closing events with timestamps to a file named `gate_log.txt`. On receipt of SIGINT, the program cleanly releases the I2C handle, shuts down the driver, stops the PWM, and closes the log file.

