This C program reads the differential pressure from a Honeywell Zephyr HAF Series HAFBLF0100A2AX5 digital airflow sensor over the I2C bus, samples the sensor every 100 ms, computes the corresponding flow rate, and drives a PWM fan connected to GPIO18 (BCM numbering) using hardware PWM at a frequency of 25 kHz. It logs each measurement to a file named `flow_log.txt` in the format "timestamp,pressure_Pa\n". The program includes robust handling of I2C communication failures by logging errors to stderr without crashing, and must clean up gracefully on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by turning off the fan, closing the I2C handle, flushing and closing the log file, and terminating the driver library.

