This C program continuously reads airflow data from a Honeywell HAF Series HAFUHH0025PA3 flow sensor over the I2C bus, samples once every second, extracts a 14-bit flow value and a 12-bit temperature value from a single 4-byte read, handles the first two reads after power-up which may return stale data, writes each timestamped measurement in SLPM and °C to a file named `flow_log.txt`, and detects I2C communication failures such as sensor disconnection or bus errors, logs any read error, attempts to re-initialize the I2C handle, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM cleanly closes the I2C handles, closes the log file, and terminates the driver library.

