This code sets up a PID-controlled reflow oven using a MAX6675 thermocouple amplifier and a solid-state relay on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the temperature from the thermocouple at a 1 Hz rate, updates the SSR duty cycle based on the PID output, logs each temperature reading to a file named `reflow_log.csv`, and loads the target temperature profile from `profile.txt`. It includes robust error handling for SPI communication and GPIO control, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path by handling termination signals.

