This C program implements a PID-controlled greenhouse heater using a DS18B20 temperature sensor and a 12V heater driven through a relay and hardware PWM on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the temperature sensor periodically, validates the CRC, handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions, computes the PID output, sets the appropriate PWM duty cycle and relay state, and logs the data every 5 seconds to a file named `greenhouse.log`. It also installs SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers to ensure resources are released on any exit path.

