This C program reads the relative humidity from an HTU21D sensor connected to the I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1` on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It polls the sensor every 60 seconds, formats the reading as a JSON document, and sends it to `http://api.example.com/humidity` using an HTTP POST request. The program uses `syslog` for logging and handles errors for I2C communication and HTTP transmission. It also catches `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to perform a graceful shutdown.

