This C program fulfills the requirements by dynamically controlling a PWM-driven cooling fan based on temperature readings from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier connected on SPI0. It reads the temperature every second, computes the duty cycle using a piecewise fan curve, and stores each timestamp, temperature, and PWM duty cycle in a 20-entry circular buffer. It performs robust error checking for every driver library call and handles SIGINT to stop the PWM, close the SPI interface, print the full contents of the circular buffer, terminate the driver library, and then exit.

