This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to communicate with a BMP180 sensor on I2C bus 1, configures GPIO2 as a falling-edge interrupt with the internal pull-up enabled, and toggles data logging each time the interrupt occurs. The main loop polls at one-second intervals, and when logging is active, it reads the sensor using an oversampling setting of OSS=3, verifies that the calibration data is successfully read, obtains temperature in Celsius and pressure in Pascals, and appends a line to an `altitude_log.txt` CSV file containing the timestamp, temperature, and pressure. It checks every I2C read and write operation for errors and handles such errors gracefully. On receipt of SIGINT, it closes the I2C handle, closes the log file, and releases the GPIO before exiting.

