This C program reads temperature from a MAX31865 RTD-to-digital converter over SPI0 using chip-enable CE0 (GPIO8) at 1 MHz, operates the device in 3-wire RTD mode with the bias voltage enabled, checks the fault status register on each read, computes the temperature using the Callendar-Van Dusen equation, and logs the results every 5 seconds to a file named `rtd_log.csv` containing a timestamp and the temperature. It includes robust error handling that logs SPI communication failures, sensor-absent conditions, and any read errors without crashing, and it performs a graceful shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by properly closing the SPI device file descriptor and the log file.

