This code provides a basic framework for interfacing with a BMP180 sensor on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the sensor's calibration data, computes pressure, and logs the data to a file when logging is enabled via a GPIO interrupt. It handles errors and cleans up resources on exit. Note that the compensation formulas for temperature and pressure are not implemented in this example and should be added based on the BMP180 datasheet.

