This C program interfaces with two Sensirion SLF3S-1300F liquid flow sensors on I2C bus 1, polls each sensor once per second, reads three bytes from each (two data bytes followed by a CRC-8 byte), validates the checksum, and retries up to three times on any I2C error before giving up on that read. When a valid reading is obtained, it appends a line to `flow_log.txt` in the specified format, skipping the entry if the CRC check fails. It also handles a clean shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by closing all I2C handles and terminating the driver library.

