This C program sets up two GPIO lines (GPIO17 and GPIO18) as open-drain outputs with internal pull-up resistors enabled. It then continuously reads the state of these lines, updating a 2-bit quadrature state machine to calculate the angular position of a magnetic rotary encoder. The calculated angle is logged to a file named `encoder_log.txt`. The program handles errors during GPIO initialization and file I/O operations, and it ensures that all resources are released when the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

