This C program reads the RPM from a Melexis MLX90254 magnetic speed sensor by counting its pulses on the GPIO bus using GPIO18 (physical pin 12) configured as an input with a pull-down resistor. It counts only rising edges and calculates the RPM over a 1-second interval. The pulse counter is protected with a pthread mutex shared between the interrupt service routine and the main thread. Each RPM value is logged together with a timestamp to `rpm_log.txt` in append mode, flushing the file immediately. Error handling checks the driver library initialization, ISR registration, and log file opening. A signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM performs a graceful shutdown by terminating the driver library, closing the log file, and destroying the mutex. It also handles the case of a missing sensor by logging 0.00 RPM when no pulses are detected.

