This C program continuously monitors a SainSmart TTP223B capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO 17 (BCM numbering, physical pin 11) on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO line. The program polls the sensor every 100ms based on CLOCK_MONOTONIC. When the sensor's output remains HIGH for more than 5 seconds, it prints an intrusion alert to stdout and resets the timer when the sensor is released. It checks every library call for failure and prints `strerror(errno)` on error. If a sensor read fails mid-loop, it prints an error and exits with `EXIT_FAILURE` after performing cleanup. The cleanup routine is also invoked on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM to gracefully release the line and close the chip on all exit paths.

