This C program continuously monitors a SainSmart IR Flame Sensor Module connected to GPIO4 (BCM) on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the digital output every 50 ms, applies a 50 ms software debounce, and starts a hardware PWM signal at 100 Hz on GPIO18 (BCM) to drive a cooling fan when a flame is detected. It logs each event to a file named `flame_log.txt` with ISO-8601 timestamps. The program handles errors, verifies successful initialization, checks the result of every GPIO read, detects a sensor-absent condition, and cleanly stops the PWM, resets the GPIO pins, terminates the driver library, and closes the log file on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

