This C program reads the state of an 8-channel TTP226 touch sensor connected to GPIO pins 2 through 9 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It polls the sensor every 100 ms, prints the timestamped state of each channel to the console, and handles errors gracefully. The program also catches SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to perform a clean shutdown, ensuring all resources are released.

