This C program initializes the pigpio library and sets up the GPIO pins for the two sensors and the LED. It then enters a loop where it polls the sensor outputs every 100 ms. If either sensor reads LOW (indicating an obstacle), it turns the LED on. If both sensors read HIGH, it turns the LED off. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to allow for graceful shutdown. On exit, it ensures that the LED is turned off and all resources are released.

