This code sets up a GPIO pin on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read pulses from a Melexis MLX90217 Hall-effect sensor. It uses the libgpiod library to configure the GPIO pin as an input with an internal pull-up resistor enabled. The program counts rising-edge pulses using GPIO interrupts and calculates the RPM based on the pulse count in a one-second window. It logs the RPM to a file named `rpm_log.txt` and prints it to stdout, flushing the file after each write. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to clean up resources and exit gracefully.

