This C program interfaces with an Omron D7S-A0011 seismic sensor on I2C bus 1, polls the sensor every 100 ms, detects earthquake-like events, logs them, and turns on an alert LED for 1 second. It handles I2C communication errors and sensor-absent conditions with up to three retries per read. On receipt of Ctrl+C/SIGINT, it cleanly releases the I2C handle, the driver library, and closes the log file.

