This C program continuously monitors five Keyes KY-026 flame sensors connected to the GPIO bus of a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It polls each sensor once per second, checks for a transition from HIGH to LOW, performs a 50 ms debounce read, and logs the event if a flame is detected. It uses the `libgpiod` library for GPIO operations and `syslog` for logging. The program handles errors gracefully, releasing resources on all exit paths and installing signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

