This C program continuously reads the TTP223 capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO4 (BCM numbering, physical pin 7) on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses the libgpiod library to configure the GPIO pin as an input with a pull-down bias and polls the pin with a debounce interval of approximately 50 ms to detect press and release transitions. Each time a touch is detected or released, it appends a line to a file named `touch_log.txt` in the exact format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS: Touch Detected" or "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS: Touch Released", flushing the file after every write. It verifies every driver call and prints a diagnostic message to stderr on failure. If the log file cannot be opened, the program releases all GPIO resources before exiting with a non-zero status. Additionally, it handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by releasing the GPIO line, closing the log file, and exiting cleanly.

