This C program fulfills the requirements by using the `libgpiod` library to handle GPIO operations on a Raspberry Pi 5. It polls four Keywish KY-033 4-Way Infrared Tracking Module sensors connected to GPIO pins 17, 18, 27, and 22 (BCM numbering). It reads the active-low outputs every 100 milliseconds, timestamps the readings, and appends them to a CSV file named `tracking_log.csv`. The program includes error handling for initialization, reading GPIO values, and file operations. It also gracefully handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals to ensure proper cleanup and resource release.

