This C program continuously samples the analog output of a TDK InvenSense ICS-40180 analog MEMS microphone connected to GPIO4 (BCM, physical pin 7) by polling the pin as a digital input at roughly 8 kHz (a 125 µs period). It treats any HIGH reading as a sound-peak event, prints a millisecond-precision timestamp to stdout for each detected peak, and for each peak turns on an LED wired with an appropriate current-limiting resistor on GPIO17 (BCM, physical pin 11) for exactly 100 ms. It checks the return value of every library API call and reports any errors to stderr. It employs a volatile `sig_atomic_t` flag to catch SIGINT, and on receiving that signal cleanly stops the sampling loop, ensures the LED is turned OFF, and invokes the library's shutdown API call.

