This C program continuously reads ambient light from up to three BH1750 I2C light sensors on I2C bus 1, averages the valid readings, and uses the result to smoothly adjust the global brightness of an APA102 RGB LED strip driven over hardware SPI. It handles errors, missing sensors, and bus errors gracefully, and installs a SIGINT handler to turn off the LED strip, close all I2C handles, close the SPI handle, and terminate the driver library on every exit path.

