This C program reads the ambient light from a BH1750 digital light sensor connected to the I2C bus (`/dev/i2c-1`) on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It stores the last 60 lux readings in a circular buffer, computes the average lux, and blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 (BCM) with a 50% duty-cycle square wave whose frequency varies proportionally from 0.5 Hz in darkness to 5 Hz at bright levels (1000 + lux). If a sensor read fails, it prints an error, skips that sample, and attempts a new read on the next loop iteration. On program termination via Ctrl-C, it catches SIGINT, cleanly releases the GPIO (unexport), and closes the I2C file descriptor.

