This C program interfaces with the GY-50 L3G4200D gyroscope over I2C bus 1 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It performs a 100-sample stationary calibration at startup to compute X, Y, and Z zero-rate offsets. It then continuously reads angular velocity, applies the offsets, and logs the calibrated X, Y, Z values together with ISO-8601 timestamps to a file named `gyro_log.txt` at a 20 Hz rate (50 ms period). It appends an alert line to the same log whenever any axis exceeds 50 dps and also prints a warning to stderr for the same condition. The program verifies the result of every open, ioctl, read, and write call, detects sensor absence by reading the WHO_AM_I register and confirming the documented value, handles any I2C bus errors, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, cleanly closes the I2C file descriptor and the log file before exiting.

