This C program samples two STMicroelectronics IMP23ABSU Ultrasonic MEMS Microphone sensors connected on I2C bus 1 at a 10 ms sampling interval. It reads 16-bit signed audio samples from each sensor, timestamps each pair of samples using `CLOCK_REALTIME`, computes the time-difference-of-arrival (TDOA) between the two channels, and appends a line to a CSV-formatted file named `audio_log.dat` with the columns `sec`, `nsec`, `sensor1`, `sensor2`, `tdoa`.

The program verifies that all driver library initialization and I2C communication calls succeed, and if a sensor is absent or the bus fails, it gracefully skips that sample and retries. A `SIGINT` signal handler guarantees clean release of I2C handles, closure of the log file, and termination of the driver library on any exit path.

