This C program continuously reads the raw 16-bit signed accelerometer and gyroscope values from a TDK MPU-6886 6-axis IMU over I2C bus 1 every 50 ms. It checks every I2C system call for errors, retries any transient read failure up to three times, and handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully. The I2C file descriptor is cleanly closed on all exit paths, including when the program receives a SIGINT (Ctrl-C).

