This C program continuously monitors two TI DRV5032 digital Hall-Effect sensors connected to GPIO17 and GPIO27 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It logs the state of each sensor to a file named `conveyor_log.txt` every 50 milliseconds with millisecond-precision timestamps. When both sensors read logic 1, it prints a halt message. The program includes robust error handling for GPIO access operations and file I/O, and it gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to release all driver resources cleanly.

