This C program continuously reads calibrated magnetic field data from an Adafruit LIS3MDL Triple-Axis Magnetometer over I2C at a rate of 10 Hz, applies the fixed offset and scale calibration constants, writes each X, Y, Z sample as a comma-separated line to a single file named `magnetic_log.txt`, checks every I2C read and write for errors and retries the sensor initialization up to three times if needed, prints a metal-detector alert to stderr whenever the total field magnitude exceeds 800 mG, and installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that cleanly close both the I2C file descriptor and the log file before exiting.

