This C program continuously reads tri-axial acceleration data from an LSM303D accelerometer/magnetometer over I2C, stores each sample in a 64-entry in-memory circular buffer, and on a rising edge of the INT1 pin (connected to BCM GPIO 23, physical pin 16) dumps to the console a timestamp followed by the last ten buffered samples. It verifies the device identity register before initialization, checks every I2C read/write and file-open operation, and handles errors appropriately. On receipt of SIGINT (Ctrl-C), it gracefully disables the accelerometer, closes the I2C file descriptor, and exits cleanly.

