This C program uses the libgpiod library to control GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up two GPIO lines (GPIO17 and GPIO27) to control two solenoids, ensuring both are initially set to LOW. It then enters a loop where it alternates between setting each GPIO line HIGH for 500ms and LOW, effectively toggling the solenoids. The program also installs a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure proper cleanup and resource release when the program is interrupted.

