This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control two DC motors driven by an L298N dual motor driver on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads pre-sampled distance values for each motor, drives the motors forward when the distance is less than 50 cm, and drives them backward when the distance is 50 cm or greater. The program handles errors, SIGINT, and SIGTERM signals, and ensures graceful motor stop and driver cleanup on all exit paths.

