This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi. It sets up the GPIO pins for the L293D H-bridge driver and the buttons, configures the buttons with internal pull-up resistors, and implements a full-step two-phase drive for the 28BYJ-48 unipolar stepper motor. The program rotates the motor 512 steps clockwise on a LOCK button press and 512 steps counter-clockwise on an UNLOCK button press. It provides console feedback for each lock, unlock, and program exit event, handles driver initialization failure, checks all GPIO configuration return codes, prevents re-triggering while a button remains held, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM the motor coils are cleanly de-energized and all driver resources are released.

