This C program continuously reads edge events from a vibration sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It accepts an optional poll timeout in milliseconds as a command-line argument, defaults to 1000 ms if not provided, maintains a sliding window of the last five events, and prints an "EARTHQUAKE ALERT" message when three or more of those events are HIGH. It logs every edge event to a file named `vibration_events.log` with an ISO-8601 timestamp and the raw value (0 or 1), handling any file open or write errors gracefully. It also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to exit cleanly, releasing the GPIO line and closing the log file.

