This C program implements a smart irrigation system for a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the libgpiod library to control GPIO pins and writes logs to a file. The program generates a random soil moisture level every 10 seconds and activates relays if the moisture level is below 30. It handles signals for clean shutdown and ensures that GPIO lines are requested as outputs only once.

