This C program reads angular velocity data from an InvenSense MPU-6050 gyroscope connected to the SPI bus on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It stores each sample in a circular buffer and blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 when any axis exceeds ±200 deg/s. On receiving SIGINT (Ctrl-C), it gracefully shuts down by releasing SPI and GPIO resources and prints the circular buffer as CSV.

