This C program initializes the MPR121 capacitive touch controller on I2C bus 1, reads touch status every 10 ms, debounces touch events with a 100 ms delay, and toggles a 5V relay connected to GPIO17 (BCM) each time electrode 0 is touched. It initializes GPIO17 to a default LOW state, checks every initialization step and every I2C operation for errors, logs all errors with timestamps to a file named `touch_relay.log`, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to cleanly close the I2C interface, release the GPIO pin, and close the log file.

