This C program continuously monitors a KY-026 flame sensor connected to GPIO17 (BCM) on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. When three consecutive reads spaced 50 ms apart all indicate a LOW level, it logs a timestamp and the text "Flame Detected" to a file named `flame_log.txt`, activates a buzzer on GPIO18 (BCM) and an LED on GPIO23 (BCM), and keeps them active as long as the sensor remains LOW. It handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to gracefully release the GPIO lines and close the log file, and ensures that all resources are released on any error exit path.

