This C program simulates sunrise and sunset lighting by controlling four independent 5V relay modules attached to lamps via the GPIO bus on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It uses the libgpiod library to manage the GPIO lines and handles errors gracefully. The program runs indefinitely, cycling through sunrise, daytime, sunset, and nighttime phases, with the relays toggling in a PWM-like manner during sunrise and sunset. On receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, the program turns off all relays and cleanly releases the GPIO resources.

