This C program continuously monitors an IR obstacle avoidance sensor connected to GPIO 17 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It debounces the input by enforcing a minimum interval of 200 ms between successive triggers. When a valid trigger occurs, it starts a 5-second video capture using `raspivid`, saving the file under `/home/pi/videos/` with a filename based on the current timestamp. It also appends a line to `/home/pi/logs/motion_log.txt` containing an ISO 8601 timestamp for the motion event. The program verifies that the sensor driver is successfully initialized, checks that all file operations succeed, and confirms that the system command for video capture executes without error. It installs a SIGINT handler that, on interruption, cleanly releases all resources by closing the log file and terminating the driver before exiting.

