This C program reads acceleration data from the Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer on the Raspberry Pi 5 using the I2C bus. It accepts optional command-line arguments for the I2C address and a threshold value. The program logs to `/var/log/high_acceleration.log` when any axis exceeds the threshold and then initiates a system shutdown. It handles errors gracefully and installs a SIGINT handler for clean termination.

