This C program continuously monitors a Seeed Studio Rain Sensor v1.0 connected to GPIO 17 (BCM) on a Raspberry Pi 5. It uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO lines. The program detects a rising edge (dry-to-wet transition) and, on that edge, starts a motor window actuator sequence using an L298N driver. It logs all events using syslog and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown.

