This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control a hobby servo connected to GPIO 18 (physical pin 12, BCM 18) based on two momentary push-buttons connected to GPIO 21 (lock button) and GPIO 22 (unlock button). It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up internal pull-up resistors, and installs a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to stop the servo and exit gracefully. The program polls the buttons in a tight loop, debounces the button presses, and sends appropriate pulse widths to the servo to lock or unlock the door. It also outputs status messages to stdout for lock, unlock, and shutdown events, and verifies the success of the API calls.

