This code sets up the necessary GPIO pins for PWM and direction control of two DC motors and quadrature encoders. It initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins, and registers interrupt service routines (ISRs) for the encoder phases. The `control_loop` function calculates the RPM of each motor based on the encoder ticks, adjusts the PWM duty cycle to maintain the target RPM, and checks for motor stalls. The program handles SIGINT by stopping the motors and releasing all resources.

