This C program continuously monitors ambient light using a BH1750 light sensor on I2C bus 1, controls a 12V LED strip through a relay connected to GPIO 17 (BCM, active-high), and logs the sensor readings and relay state changes to a file named `chicken_coop_log.txt`. It activates the relay at dusk when lux falls below 50 and deactivates it at dawn when lux rises above 200, with hysteresis to avoid rapid toggling. It includes comprehensive error handling for driver initialization, I2C communication, and file I/O. All resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including graceful shutdown when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

