This C program initializes the MPR121 capacitive touch sensor on the Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the I2C bus 1, sets up the necessary GPIO for the relay, and continuously polls the sensor every 50 ms. It logs the relay state changes to a file named `relay_log.txt` with timestamps. The program includes comprehensive error handling and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including handling a SIGINT (Ctrl-C) signal.

