This C program initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIO pins 17 and 27 as outputs, and then enters an infinite loop where it generates random haptic feedback patterns for the two motors. Each pattern consists of a random number of steps (between 5 and 15), with each step having a random PWM duty cycle (0 to 255) and a random duration (50 to 200 milliseconds). The program gracefully handles memory allocation failures, checks the return values of API calls, and releases all resources when a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) is received.

