This C program continuously monitors a weight-triggered solenoid lock using a load cell amplified by an HX711 on the GPIO bus. It reads the HX711 sensor every 500 ms, enforces a read timeout of 0.5 seconds, initializes the GPIO driver with error checking, loads calibration data from a `calibration.txt` file or falls back to defaults, performs a one-time startup calibration, computes weight using the loaded or default scale and offset, engages the solenoid when the computed weight exceeds a calibrated threshold of 10.0 kg, logs each reading with a timestamp to `weight_log.txt`, writes any updated calibration values back to `calibration.txt`, and handles SIGINT to cleanly shut down by releasing all GPIO resources and closing open files.

