This C program continuously monitors a Seeed Studio Grove Rain Sensor connected to GPIO4 (BCM) on the GPIO bus. It debounces the sensor by taking five readings spaced 50 ms apart and declares rain when at least three of those readings are LOW. When rain is detected, it drives a DC motor through an L298N motor driver using IN1 on GPIO17 (BCM), IN2 on GPIO18 (BCM), and the PWM enable line on GPIO27 (BCM), setting IN1 high, IN2 low, and applying a 1000 Hz PWM signal with a duty cycle value of 150 (out of 0-255) for exactly five seconds to close the window, then stopping the motor by clearing IN1, IN2, and PWM. It logs each rain event and each motor action with timestamps to `/var/log/window_control.log` via syslog, checking the sensor only once every 60 seconds and waiting an additional 60 seconds after a closing operation before the next check. It handles any GPIO initialization failures with clear error messages and distinct exit codes, provides robust error handling for all sensor reads and motor control actions, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM the motor is stopped, all GPIO resources are released, and the log file is properly closed for a graceful shutdown.

