This C program continuously reads illuminance from a BH1750 light sensor on I2C bus 1, observes a 180 ms measurement delay, and drives a relay connected to GPIO23 (BCM) to turn on a grow lamp whenever the lux reading falls below 150. It logs each lux value and every relay state change with millisecond-precision timestamps to a file named `grow_log.txt`. The program handles I2C errors gracefully by logging any sensor detection or read failures and continuing operation without crashing. It runs indefinitely until a SIGINT is received, at which point it cleanly releases all resources by closing the I2C handle, turning off the relay, and terminating the driver library.

