This C program continuously reads the ambient light from a BH1750 light sensor attached to the I2C bus (/dev/i2c-1) once every second, converts the 16-bit big-endian raw value to a floating-point lux value, and broadcasts that value as a floating-point string via UDP multicast to 239.255.255.250:5000 with a TTL of 1. It checks every I2C write and read operation for failure, and if the sensor is absent or a bus error occurs, it prints an error message and retries after one second. It also installs a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM that cleanly closes the I2C file descriptor and the socket before exiting.

