This C program interfaces with a Texas Instruments AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor over UART (`/dev/ttyS0`) at 921600 baud. It reads the sensor's data stream, synchronizes on the documented 8-byte little-endian magic word, validates each TLV payload, extracts the range (in meters) and velocity (in meters per second) for every detected object, and appends rows to a file named `radar_data.csv` with the columns `timestamp`, `object_index`, `range_m`, `velocity_mps`. It checks every UART read, handles partial reads and buffer overflows gracefully, skips malformed frames, logs any errors to stderr without crashing, and on all exit paths including SIGINT or SIGTERM cleanly releases resources by closing the UART using the provided driver library, flushing and closing the CSV file, and invoking the library's `call()` cleanup function.

